Translation patch: <RistrettoPoint as MultiscalarMul>::multiscalar_mul (src/ristretto.rs)

Change: The lazy `points.into_iter().map(|P| P.borrow().0)` passed to `EdwardsPoint::multiscalar_mul`
becomes a `Vec<EdwardsPoint>` built by a nested helper.

Why: the Aeneas Lean library models only `Iterator::next`; the provided methods
(`map`, `zip`, `fold`, `filter`, `collect`, `rev`, `skip`, `size_hint`, `by_ref`, ...)
are missing (AeneasVerif/aeneas#1057), so the original does not build in Lean.
Aeneas also cannot extract a loop that calls `next()` directly on the `IntoIter` of a
generic `IntoIterator` parameter ("Could not find: type_var_id .. from ExtractBase.Item"),
so the consuming loop lives in a nested helper function generic over `It: Iterator`,
called with `x.into_iter()`.

Behaviour: **not identical on its own; same result for valid inputs.** The callee receives the same
points in the same order, so for exact-size iterators of equal length the result is the
same. Judged without edwards-multiscalar_mul.patch, the callee's `size_hint` asserts (see
below) now see the exact `Vec` length instead of the caller's hint: inputs with inexact hints
(e.g. `filter`), which panicked before, now succeed; iterators with inaccurate hints may
panic where they did not, or vice versa; an infinite points iterator, which panicked before,
now does not terminate. The points are read (and the points iterator dropped) before
`scalars.into_iter()` is called; the original read them after `scalars.into_iter()` and
both `size_hint` calls, but still before any scalar. With edwards-multiscalar_mul.patch also
applied (as in the translation), the combined behaviour is the one declared there.

Facts relied on (not visible in the diff): `EdwardsPoint::multiscalar_mul` (unpatched) calls `size_hint()` on both iterators
and `assert_eq!`s that they are exact and equal, then (`straus_multiscalar_mul`) collects
all points before reading any scalar. With edwards-multiscalar_mul.patch also applied (as in
the translation) those `size_hint` asserts are replaced by an exact length check.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
index 269662d..a3f6f18 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
@@ -968,13 +968,25 @@ impl MultiscalarMul for RistrettoPoint {
     fn multiscalar_mul<I, J>(scalars: I, points: J) -> RistrettoPoint
     where
         I: IntoIterator,
         I::Item: Borrow<Scalar>,
         J: IntoIterator,
         J::Item: Borrow<RistrettoPoint>,
     {
-        let extended_points = points.into_iter().map(|P| P.borrow().0);
+        fn extended_points<It>(mut points: It) -> Vec<EdwardsPoint>
+        where
+            It: Iterator,
+            It::Item: Borrow<RistrettoPoint>,
+        {
+            let mut out = Vec::new();
+            while let Some(P) = points.next() {
+                out.push(P.borrow().0);
+            }
+            out
+        }
+
+        let extended_points = extended_points(points.into_iter());
         RistrettoPoint(EdwardsPoint::multiscalar_mul(scalars, extended_points))
     }
 }
 
